WEBVTT

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.000
Wow, you like WIXOSS?

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.140
I'm pretty persistent!

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.160
Kiyoi, you're really funny, 
the way you look so sulky.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.440
Nice to meet you,

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:55.180
Kominato Ruuko-san.

00:01:57.260 --> 00:01:58.220
Huh?

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:01.010
I suppose this isn't our first meeting, is it?

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:04.600
We've met before, as Selector and LRIG.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:07.940
I need to talk to you.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:10.650
What?

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:13.050
The Selector battles aren't over?

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:13.770
Indeed.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:15.640
But that's impossible, because...

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:17.780
Because Mayu is gone, right?

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:26.830
Mayu, a girl whose short life ended 
before she ever saw the outside world.

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:31.790
Her emotions came to dwell within the 
cards, creating the first Selector battle.

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:33.750
And Mayu is...

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:38.040
Mayu is still there, inside that white room?

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:40.970
No, Mayu is gone.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:45.190
You saved her.

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:46.460
Right?

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:48.770
But the battles haven't ended.

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:52.460
The emotions of all those 
lost and tormented girls

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:54.920
have put the next set of gears in motion.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:56.780
An endless cycle of darkness...

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:58.740
And I want to stop it.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.160
Stop the cycle?

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:02.240
Help me.

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:05.580
You released all the LRIGs, so with your help...

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:06.850
I'm sorry!

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:11.000
I... I can't help you.

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:13.460
I have a friend I care about.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:15.380
One who means everything to me.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:19.020
If I get involved, I'm sure she'll...

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:22.680
I don't want her to fight any more battles!

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:24.220
I see.

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:31.460
A friend she cares about...

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:33.190
Kiyoi!

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:38.150
Amika?

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:41.360
Jeez! Why don't you answer your phone?

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:43.380
Where were you?

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:44.820
I'm not telling you.

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:47.200
Visiting another former Selector?

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:53.060
Jeez... I keep telling you to stop.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:55.790
I know. That's why I turned off my phone.

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:57.640
Come on...

00:03:57.640 --> 00:03:59.050
You don't need to worry.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:01.720
Of course I'll worry.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:05.300
My friend keeps trying to get 
involved in a dangerous game.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:08.800
Why do you have to do this?

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:11.260
Maybe you hurt those girls,

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:13.270
but it's not your fault alone.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.730
Just stop.

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:17.950
Thank you.

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:19.800
But I can't.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.330
Is this about Sakaguchi-san?

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:22.090
Yes.

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:24.070
But it's not just that.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:29.450
If I do nothing, my meeting with 
you will become a lie, as well.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.730
You're an LRIG that brings misery, aren't you?

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:37.470
You bring misery to every Selector you meet.

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:41.920
Like that girl, Aoi Akira...

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:46.830
I don't want to hear that from someone 
who's enjoying watching it happen.

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:48.600
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.910
I love you.

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:55.140
No one comes here as often as you do.

00:04:56.260 --> 00:05:00.430
Each time you do, 
another girl's wish is crushed.

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:07.390
And you're starting to feel 
nothing when you crush them.

00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:09.580
It's wonderful.

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:13.460
Who will you destroy next?

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:16.300
Like you did to that girl, Sakaguchi...

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:20.680
I can't wait to find out.

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:34.250
Um... "This LRIG will be your avatar"?

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:42.320
I don't get it.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:44.820
Sakaguchi?

00:05:46.670 --> 00:05:48.290
"Piruluk"...

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:50.660
Are you the one who'll grant my wish?

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:52.410
That is an acceptable assessment.

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:55.690
Win enough battles, and 
your wish will come true.

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:58.830
Can the wish be for someone besides me?

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:01.660
As long as it is what you truly wish.

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:05.590
My mom is sick.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:10.270
If I wish to save her, 
will that wish come true?

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:14.010
If you win enough battles...

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:16.480
<i>Her face reminded me of Sakaguchi.</i>

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:18.440
<i>That was all there was to her,</i>

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:20.900
<i>or so I thought at first.</i>

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:22.240
<i>But...</i>

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:27.060
I was so scared when 
I found out Mom was sick.

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:30.450
I was so worried, and 
I couldn't talk to anyone.

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:35.160
That's why I was so happy when 
I had you to talk to, Piruluk.

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:40.000
And you know, I liked you 
the first time I saw you.

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:42.630
It's funny how your face looks so sulky.

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:48.720
Wait, no! I meant sulky in a cute way!

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:54.510
<i>LRIGs have no special powers.</i>

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:57.860
<i>Get rid of me, and stop participating 
in the Selector battles.</i>

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:13.320
Huh? Is that you, Kiyoi-chan?

00:07:13.730 --> 00:07:15.030
Remember!

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:16.440
Kiyoi?

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:18.320
It's been so long!

00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:20.240
She's a Selector now?

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:23.080
What? What do you mean, Piruluk?

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:27.040
Oh, so your name's Piruluk now?

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:31.040
This body was originally hers.

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:32.840
Her name was Mizushima Kiyoi-chan.

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:36.840
I was Kiyoi-chan's LRIG.

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:40.150
Kiyoi-chan won enough battles 
to become an Eternal Girl.

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:42.100
Then she switched places with me.

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:43.560
Switched places?

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:49.410
As the price for their wish coming 
true, Selectors become LRIGs.

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:51.960
That's the rule.

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:52.760
That can't be...

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:55.800
Oh, but don't worry.

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:59.790
The LRIG that takes their 
place will grant their wish.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:05.920
I granted Kiyoi-chan's wish.

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:08.500
It was, "I want to save my hospitalized friend."

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:10.130
Right, Kiyoi-chan?

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:14.860
You have a wish, too, don't you?

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:16.090
So let's battle.

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:17.610
Huh, but...

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:18.470
We were lucky enough to meet each other...

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:18.470
Amika, no!

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:21.740
You've lost twice! 
If you lose one more time...

00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:26.060
Hello, Dad? What is it?

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:28.790
Mom is...

00:08:30.100 --> 00:08:32.300
Okay. I'll get to the hospital right away!

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:33.280
Amika...

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:35.720
But first...

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:38.200
Let's do it.

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:40.910
Amika, get rid of me!

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:42.790
I want to save my mom!

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:43.910
Open!

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:55.750
<i>Even if you trade places with an LRIG, 
your wish won't come true.</i>

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:58.810
<i>And if you lose three times, 
the opposite of your wish occurs.</i>

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:00.140
<i>Which means...</i>

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:04.940
<i>It'll be impossible to save her mother.</i>

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:10.580
Liar...

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:13.530
You lied to me?

00:09:13.730 --> 00:09:15.400
I believed in you!

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:17.110
Why?

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:23.700
I've sacrificed many Selectors 
to get revenge on Remember.

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:25.710
You're just another one of them.

00:09:26.190 --> 00:09:29.170
But when I met you, I wavered.

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:32.420
Because you were just like Sakaguchi.

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:36.950
I should've just left you sooner...

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:39.270
but I couldn't!

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:44.300
Because I felt like I never 
wanted to leave you...

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:49.610
I'm sorry, Amika.

00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:51.090
Piruluk...

00:09:56.970 --> 00:09:58.740
I'm changing my wish.

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:01.300
I want to save my mother.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:03.910
But if that's impossible,

00:10:05.260 --> 00:10:08.550
I want to make you human again!

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:10.750
Because you're my friend.

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:13.710
Amika...

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:16.780
Oh, is that all you want for your wish?

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:19.590
Either way, I'm going to win, though!

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:28.620
Attack!

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:36.490
Piruluk, grow!

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:43.080
Level 5?

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:52.890
The battle ends with this turn, Amika.

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:57.010
Will you believe in me just one more time?

00:10:57.310 --> 00:10:59.840
Okay, Kiyoi.

00:11:02.420 --> 00:11:04.010
Peeping Analyze!

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:10.440
Turn end.

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:12.030
She's not attacking?

00:11:12.030 --> 00:11:14.770
I don't know what she's after, but...

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:21.540
I'm going to take an easy win, then!

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:25.820
Kiyoi!

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:30.580
She just threw away her win?

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:38.210
The level-up turned Peeping Analyze into 
the power to change someone's will.

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:42.470
I took over Amika's mind 
and rewrote her wish.

00:11:42.670 --> 00:11:46.300
Her new wish is "I want to lose my mother."

00:11:46.540 --> 00:11:49.770
The Selector battle rules 
are merciless and definite.

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:52.230
With her loss, the opposite 
of her wish will come true.

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:56.190
She'll never lose her mother!

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:01.180
You threw away your only chance?

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:03.070
Are you stupid?

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:06.640
Well, I doubt we'll ever see 
each other again, though.

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:08.340
So long!

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:44.400
I feel betrayed.

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:48.700
I simply managed to get what I 
wanted while sticking to the rules.

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:51.240
I need to punish you.

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:56.420
How about I just erase you from existence?

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:56.960
I see.

00:12:58.550 --> 00:13:00.230
You don't seem scared at all.

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:02.460
You'll disappear! You'll be annihilated!

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:05.860
I've hurt many young girls.

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:08.520
I need to be punished for that.

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:09.680
You're crazy!

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:14.540
Why aren't you screaming, "I don't want
to disappear! I don't want to die!"?

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:17.180
It doesn't matter anymore.

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:21.530
I granted Amika's wish.

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:25.450
You remind me, I think,

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:28.840
of what I was until a short time ago.

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:31.440
Always alone, unable to believe anyone.

00:13:31.440 --> 00:13:34.170
Feeding off nothing but revenge.

00:13:34.170 --> 00:13:38.080
But deep down in your heart, 
you want to be saved.

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:40.400
I met Amika.

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:41.620
Someday, you, too...

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:42.730
I hate you.

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:44.510
I hate you, I hate you!

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:45.990
I hate you, I hate you!

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:48.090
I <i>hate</i> you!

00:13:51.940 --> 00:13:56.310
You're going to suffer for ruining my game!

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:12.530
Kiyoi?

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:15.120
Amika...

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:26.380
Your meeting with me would become a lie?

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:29.870
The girl named Sakaguchi Ayumi...

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:33.820
Since I lost my memories, 
you told me about her many times.

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:37.830
Oh, that's a WIXOSS novel!

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:40.880
Wow, you like WIXOSS?

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:42.860
Let's have a battle sometime! Okay?

00:14:43.730 --> 00:14:46.560
I think this'll work for a deck.

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:48.960
I sure wish I could battle someone.

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:51.780
Knock it off.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:56.500
I decided I wouldn't give up 
until I played WIXOSS with you.

00:14:57.670 --> 00:14:59.290
I'm pretty persistent!

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:02.080
Why?

00:15:02.720 --> 00:15:05.740
You have lots of friends.

00:15:05.740 --> 00:15:07.060
You don't need me...

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:10.040
I want to play you, Kiyoi.

00:15:12.790 --> 00:15:16.750
Kiyoi, you're really funny, 
the way you look so sulky.

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:21.880
I always thought it would be fun to 
talk to you about all kinds of things.

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:27.860
But if you really don't want to, 
I can't force you.

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:32.030
I guess one game would be okay...

00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:37.550
Mizushima-san's always ignored Ayumi, 
but now that Ayumi's ready to give up,

00:15:37.550 --> 00:15:40.170
she finally agrees to battle.

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:43.260
Why not just say she wants to be friends?

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:44.580
It's creepy.

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:46.930
Wait!

00:15:46.930 --> 00:15:48.160
Hey, Kiyoi!

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:49.750
Did I do something wrong?

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:52.630
I was looking forward to our battle.

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:56.620
I thought you'd give up 
if I said just one time.

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:58.630
You really are persistent.

00:15:58.630 --> 00:15:59.900
Kiyoi?

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:03.180
I don't like WIXOSS, and 
I don't like people like you!

00:16:07.460 --> 00:16:08.190
Kiyoi!

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:20.990
Hello, Selector.

00:16:20.990 --> 00:16:22.540
I'm Remember.

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:24.750
I'm here to grant your wish.

00:16:27.150 --> 00:16:28.250
My wish?

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:34.220
My wish is... to save Sakaguchi!

00:16:35.810 --> 00:16:37.880
I accept...

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:39.810
I accept...

00:16:39.810 --> 00:16:41.470
The laws of the Selector.

00:16:51.080 --> 00:16:53.130
Remember, what are you doing?

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:56.870
Sakaguchi-san, rest in peace, okay?

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:06.210
She was released from suffering...

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:07.920
through death.

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:09.250
No...

00:17:09.560 --> 00:17:10.870
Congratulations.

00:17:10.870 --> 00:17:13.240
Your wish came true.

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:19.650
It was my fault Sakaguchi 
was in that accident,

00:17:19.650 --> 00:17:21.520
and my fault that Remember killed her,

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:25.020
but now I feel nothing about that.

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:26.200
Kiyoi?

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:29.270
I'm not the real me anymore.

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:31.800
If I remain fake forever,

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:33.540
I can never face you.

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:36.030
I want to truly be your friend.

00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:39.740
I can't stop you, can I?

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:47.360
I want to get my memories back.

00:17:47.360 --> 00:17:49.750
I want to atone for the past.

00:17:49.980 --> 00:17:51.710
These are my personal reasons.

00:17:52.270 --> 00:17:55.500
Everyone has to face this 
for their own reasons.

00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:58.620
I'm home!

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:01.710
Welcome back, Ruu-chan.

00:18:03.530 --> 00:18:04.660
Ruu!

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:09.230
Welcome back, Ruu!

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:11.230
I'm home, Tama.

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:13.140
Oh, my.

00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:14.280
I'm home, Grandma.

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:17.620
Dinner tonight is meat and 
potato stew, your favorite.

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:18.760
Beef and potato!

00:18:18.760 --> 00:18:20.240
That's great!

00:18:24.350 --> 00:18:25.360
Why?

00:18:30.070 --> 00:18:31.210
Who's there?

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:33.920
Who are you?

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:34.710
Who?

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:35.690
An LRIG.

00:18:35.690 --> 00:18:36.550
An LRIG, right?

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:37.480
Who's there?

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:38.680
Me.

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:40.300
I am no one.

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:44.580
I am this room itself.

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:47.600
I am Eternal.

00:18:48.240 --> 00:18:49.560
Eternal?

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:53.200
What is your wish? The wish 
you want to come true?

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:54.690
Tell me your wish.

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:55.830
Wish?

00:18:56.250 --> 00:19:00.700
Hmph. I just want this boring 
world to be more exciting.

00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:03.120
Everything is here.

00:19:03.640 --> 00:19:05.070
Everything...

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:07.330
Everything...

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:08.920
What?

00:19:08.920 --> 00:19:10.680
A strong LRIG.

00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:11.790
I've been waiting.

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:13.340
I've been waiting for you.

00:19:13.340 --> 00:19:14.750
Do you want everything?

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:16.420
This room...

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:19.550
You're saying I can control 
the Selector battles?

00:19:20.640 --> 00:19:21.800
Open the door.

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:23.510
Open it.

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:25.310
You must...

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:28.510
gather the keys to open 
the door of the heart,

00:19:28.510 --> 00:19:30.810
the keys to open the door to despair.

00:19:31.280 --> 00:19:32.270
Gather them.

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:33.470
You must.

00:19:33.470 --> 00:19:34.620
We're waiting.

00:19:38.660 --> 00:19:40.880
Sounds like fun...

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:13.440
Piruluk...

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:15.580
It's been a long time, Kiyoi.

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:18.440
I see. So it's begun.

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:20.740
Yes. It's begun.

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:22.420
The Selector battle.

00:20:25.260 --> 00:20:27.240
For the next ninety days,

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:31.230
you'll battle for coins that 
are linked to your memories.

00:20:31.230 --> 00:20:34.360
You're that Piruluk?

00:20:35.050 --> 00:20:35.920
That's right.

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:40.800
You and I were chosen 
to be Selector and LRIG.

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:45.030
The old rules said that Selectors 
were chosen randomly.

00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:47.060
Is it different this time?

00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:48.510
So it seems.

00:20:48.980 --> 00:20:51.730
I have your memories within me.

00:20:51.730 --> 00:20:54.480
The treasured memories you lost.

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:57.190
Let's get them back together.

00:20:57.710 --> 00:20:58.820
Yes.

00:21:02.620 --> 00:21:03.900
What's this?

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:05.160
A key card.

00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:09.160
A new rule that was added for these battles.

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:10.740
To use it...

00:21:14.860 --> 00:21:18.080
More and more Selectors are being born...

00:21:29.240 --> 00:21:31.060
So you're Satomi?

00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:36.110
That's the name of the 
last owner of this body.

00:21:36.110 --> 00:21:38.060
Call me Carnival.

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:40.530
Huh... I like it.

00:21:40.530 --> 00:21:43.000
Then you can call me Layla.

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:44.520
So what do you want?

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:50.490
A battle that will make my blood boil.

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:55.960
Reason / Hesitation and Resolution

00:23:26.640 --> 00:23:28.790
If you want, you can talk to me about it.

00:23:28.790 --> 00:23:32.320
It didn't work out last time, 
but I'm starting over.

00:23:32.320 --> 00:23:35.000
I'm helping, too!

00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:36.520
I told you, no!

00:23:36.520 --> 00:23:38.000
Let us begin!

00:23:37.770 --> 00:23:40.980
Initiation / Usual and Unusual

00:23:38.000 --> 00:23:40.980
Initiation / Usual and Unusual.
